==Bulgarian==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|bg|de|Autobus}} or {{bor|bg|ru|авто́бус}}, ultimately from {{der|bg|fr|autobus}}. The term is a clipping of {{cog|grc|αὐτός||self}} + {{cog|la|omnibus||for everyone}} {{q|pl. dat. of {{m|la|omnis}}}}. Originally, it referred to [[automobile]]s that were capable of transporting multiple passengers, whence the element {{affix|bg|авто-}}. Previously, this service was performed by horse-chariots called in {{cog|fr|omnibus}}, whence the element {{l|bg|-бус}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{bg-IPA|автобу́с}}

===Noun===
{{bg-noun|автобу́с|m|adj=автобу́сен}}

# [[bus]], [[motorbus]]

====Declension====
{{bg-ndecl|автобу́с<(v)>}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|bg|автомоби́л||automobile}}
* {{l|bg|тролейбу́с||trolleybus}}
* {{l|bg|микробу́с||microbus}}

===References===
* {{R:bg:RBE}}
* {{R:bg:RBE2}}

{{cln|bg|words suffixed with -ус}}

